The case on both sides of the KSM mine is now a court order.

00:13:10.046 --> 00:13:15.446
The BC Supreme Court told the province to rethink a 2024 finding that Seabridge Gold's KSM

00:13:15.446 --> 00:13:20.286
project had substantially started and to consult the Tetsets out ski kilometers Laxhawn

00:13:20.286 --> 00:13:20.546
Nation.

00:13:21.086 --> 00:13:25.326
Global news calls it one of the world's largest undeveloped gold reserves in the Golden

00:13:25.326 --> 00:13:30.526
triangle and says it would be Canada's largest gold mine if it is built. Ryan Beaton of Power

00:13:30.526 --> 00:13:35.406
Law, for that nation and chief Darleen Simpson, says the province already had evidence the

00:13:35.406 --> 00:13:40.786
waste facility ground is their territory. A 2023 assessment, he said, found all the evidence

00:13:40.786 --> 00:13:45.726
pointed that way, and the court agreed Victoria said its own conclusion aside, which was a failure

00:13:45.726 --> 00:13:51.026
to consult. The nation is not against the mine. Beaton said members work in mining that they

00:13:51.026 --> 00:13:55.826
a strong economy in good projects, and that they want this one done efficiently, responsibly,

00:13:56.006 --> 00:14:00.786
and sustainably, with their rights respected. The NISGA nation and the Tahaltan nation support

00:14:00.786 --> 00:14:05.506
the project and the substantial start decision. They say they are the rights holders and the decision

00:14:05.506 --> 00:14:10.666
makers on their territories, that they do not recognize TSKLH as holding Aboriginal rights

00:14:10.666 --> 00:14:15.846
or title there, and that they reject those claims on KSM. They place the project into Halton

00:14:15.846 --> 00:14:20.646
territory, and in the NAS area and NAS wildlife area under the Nizga final agreement.

00:14:21.146 --> 00:14:24.066
They called the competing claims opportunistic and unsupported.

00:14:24.466 --> 00:14:29.126
They said BC's broader consultation habit has drawn in groups with unsupported, marginal

00:14:29.126 --> 00:14:33.886
or speculative claims, which creates uncertainty and disrespects treaty rights in the proper

00:14:33.886 --> 00:14:34.546
title holders.

00:14:35.006 --> 00:14:39.186
They are worried that habit lets groups without a rights holders duties hijack and derail

00:14:39.186 --> 00:14:39.626
reviews.

00:14:40.146 --> 00:14:45.146
The substantial start label now goes back for another look and for consultation with TSKLH.

